RECONCILIATION — declared vs extracted. These are different measurements of one record;
a gap is information about the record, not an error to smooth away.

bucket     declared  extracted  delta
─────────  ────────  ─────────  ─────
self              2         12     10
committee         5         10      5
keeper            4         39     35

  They are NOT summed anywhere, and BOTH SIGNS are expected for structural reasons.
  POSITIVE: prose attributions run back through every cycle before ledgers were being
  written at all, so an unfiltered run counts events no tally ever covered.
  NEGATIVE: a ledger's own enumerated items are deliberately held out of the event stream
  (otherwise the tally and its contents would both count), so wherever a ledger exists its
  catches are declared and not extracted. Narrowing with --since makes this the common
  case, because the windows that survive are the ones that have ledgers.
  Neither sign is evidence of a bug. A delta worth reading is one where a window has a
  ledger AND prose attributions the ledger does not account for.

