DEDUPLICATION: 1 merged · 145 events had no recoverable named subject and were LEFT SEPARATE
SUSPECTED RULE GAPS: 12 unattributed events whose sentence NAMES a
  known catcher — the record said who, and the rules did not hear it. Nothing is
  re-classified; this is the rule table auditing itself (--show suspect).
WEAK, NOT COUNTED: 115 sentences use "catch" as a noun rather than reporting an
  event ("what grows is the catch"). Scored nowhere. A real event phrased without the verb
  lives in here, so this list is meant to be read, not ignored (--show weak).

These are candidates. Every count here can be walked back to a file and line (--show <bucket>),
and a reader who disagrees with one should overrule that line, not the instrument. This file
never decides whether something was a catch — it decides where the record says one was.
